    "collapsible_content_FWm6Pt": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "accordion_LEXeqE": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does it support both the 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz bands simultaneously?",
            "answer": "<p>No, it does not support simultaneous operation of both bands. While the Numen Air is a dual-band 5G Wi-Fi device supporting both 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz bands, only one band can be active at a time. We recommend switching to 5 GHz in crowded areas to reduce interference; use 2.4 GHz when requiring longer transmission distances or connecting legacy devices.</p>",
            "opened": false
          }
        },
        "accordion_9n99Ub": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How secure is the work hotspot?",
            "answer": "<p>Users can set their own Wi-Fi password, manage connected devices via the touchscreen, restrict access to authorized personnel, and enable anti-trespassing features.</p>",
            "opened": false
          }
        },
        "accordion_eVY6gh": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will it auto switch between 5G and 4G if 5G is weak?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, it can switch networks automatically to keep the best signal so I don’t drop off during calls or uploads.</p>",
            "opened": false
          }
        },
        "accordion_qRbcqi": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What happens if I travel to a country not covered by 5G?",
            "answer": "<p>It falls back to 4G (which covers 200+ countries/regions). I’ll still have connectivity—just with 4G performance.</p>",
            "opened": false
          }
        },
        "accordion_3XmM6g": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is it truly easy to manage especially when I'm traveling between countries?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, it's designed to be very simple. You just turn it on and it's ready to use. You can manage everything through the user-friendly \"GlocalMe\" app on your phone, where you can see your real-time data usage, top up credit, and check the network status. When you travel to a new country, it will automatically connect to a local network for you, making the process completely hassle-free.</p>",
            "opened": false
          }
        },
        "accordion_XYQXwH": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How good is the signal and speed in real-world use, like inside a hotel or on a train?",
            "answer": "<p>The signal and speed depend entirely on the local cellular network coverage in your area, just like a phone. Inside buildings with thick walls, the signal may be weaker. The device will show you its signal strength. On a moving train, the connection will fluctuate as it switches between cell towers, so it's fine for browsing and email but may not be stable enough for a continuous HD video call.</p>",
            "opened": false
          }
        }
      },
